  "steps": [
    "Simmer the cider in a large pot until reduced to about 1/2 cup, thick like jelly; do not reduce further.",
    "Melt the cubed butter in a light pan over low heat, stirring, 3 minutes until the fats start to brown. Whisk in the buttermilk powder and cook 3 to 4 more minutes until golden brown. Chill until solid.",
    "Let the browned butter come to room temperature, about an hour.",
    "Whisk the flour, ClearJel, cinnamon, nutmeg, baking soda and salt together.",
    "Cream the browned butter and sugars in a stand mixer, 30 to 45 seconds. Mix in the buttermilk, then 5 tbsp cider reduction, egg, yolk and vanilla just until combined.",
    "Add the flour mixture on low until just mixed, then cover and chill overnight.",
    "Bake 60 g dough balls on parchment at 350°F for 12 to 15 minutes.",
    "While the cookies are hot, swirl a round cutter around each to push them thicker, then brush with melted butter and roll in cinnamon sugar.",
    "For the buttercream, whip the butter and shortening until fluffy, add the powdered sugar, then the cream, vanilla and caramel sauce to taste.",
    "Sandwich the cooled cookies with buttercream."
  ],
